research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/cex-limsup-infinite-not-attained-in-r.md-416-
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/cex-limsup-infinite-not-attained-in-r.md:417:**Given:** The alternating sequence $(s_k)$ and the index maps $e, o$ of [[lem-alternating-sequence]]; the canonical naturals $\iota(k) = k \cdot 1_{\mathbb{R}}$ with $\iota(0) = 0$; and the sequence $x_k := \iota(k)$ when $s_k = 1$ and $x_k := 0$ when $s_k = -1$.
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/cex-limsup-infinite-not-attained-in-r.md-418-
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/cex-limsup-infinite-not-attained-in-r.md-419-[L1] The alternating sequence: $|s_k| = 1$, $s_{e_j} = 1$, $s_{o_j} = -1$, and $e$, $o$ are strictly increasing, so $e_j \ge j$ and $o_j \ge j$ ([[lem-alternating-sequence]], [[lem-index-map-grows]]).
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/cex-limsup-infinite-not-attained-in-r.md-420-
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/cex-limsup-infinite-not-attained-in-r.md-421-[L2] Limit superior in $\overline{\mathbb{R}}$: existence for every sequence, the tail supremum being the least upper bound of the tail range and $\limsup$ the greatest lower bound of the family of tail suprema ([[def-limsup-liminf]], [[lem-limsup-exists]], [[lem-extended-reals-complete]], [[def-upper-bound]], [[def-partial-order]], [[def-sequence]]).
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/cex-limsup-infinite-not-attained-in-r.md-422-
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/cex-limsup-infinite-not-attained-in-r.md-423-[L3] The order on $\overline{\mathbb{R}}$ is total, $+\infty$ is greatest, every real is $< +\infty$ and $> -\infty$, and the order restricts on $\mathbb{R}$ to the order of $\mathbb{R}$ ([[def-extended-reals]]).
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/cex-limsup-infinite-not-attained-in-r.md-424-
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/cex-limsup-infinite-not-attained-in-r.md-425-[L4] Extended subsequential limits and convergence in $\overline{\mathbb{R}}$; divergence to $+\infty$ means that for every real $M$ one has $x_k > M$ eventually ([[def-extended-limits]], [[def-divergence-to-infinity]], [[def-subsequential-limit]], [[def-real-limit]]).
--
