research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/thm-laurent-ordered-field.md-198-1. $P$ is a positive cone on $K$, so $(K, P)$ is an ordered field
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/thm-laurent-ordered-field.md-199-   ([[def-ordered-field]]), and $f < g$ holds exactly when $g - f \ne 0_K$ and
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/thm-laurent-ordered-field.md-200-   $\operatorname{lc}(g - f) > 0$.
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/thm-laurent-ordered-field.md-201-2. For $f \ne 0_K$ the absolute value ([[def-abs-value]]) satisfies
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/thm-laurent-ordered-field.md-202-   $|f| \ne 0_K$, $v(|f|) = v(f)$ and
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/thm-laurent-ordered-field.md-203-   $\operatorname{lc}(|f|) = \lvert \operatorname{lc}(f) \rvert > 0$.
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/thm-laurent-ordered-field.md-204-3. The map $\iota : \mathbb{R} \to K$ sending $c$ to the series with value $c$
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/thm-laurent-ordered-field.md-205-   at index $0$ is an injective ring homomorphism with $\iota(c) \in P$ exactly
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/thm-laurent-ordered-field.md:206:   when $c > 0$; and the canonical naturals of $K$ are
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/thm-laurent-ordered-field.md-207-   $n \cdot 1_K = \iota(n \cdot 1_{\mathbb{R}})$ for every $n \in \mathbb{N}$.
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/thm-laurent-ordered-field.md-208-
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/thm-laurent-ordered-field.md-209-## Facts & Assumptions
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/thm-laurent-ordered-field.md-210-
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/thm-laurent-ordered-field.md-211-**Given:** $K$ with its valuation $v$, leading coefficient $\operatorname{lc}$, constants $\iota(c)$ and the set $P$ above.
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/thm-laurent-ordered-field.md-212-
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/thm-laurent-ordered-field.md-213-[L1] For nonzero $h \in K$, $h(k) = 0$ for $k < v(h)$ and $h(v(h)) = \operatorname{lc}(h) \ne 0$; $\iota(c)$ is $c$ at index $0$ and $0$ elsewhere; $1_K = \iota(1)$ ([[def-formal-laurent-series]]).
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/thm-laurent-ordered-field.md-214-
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/thm-laurent-ordered-field.md-215-[L2] $K$ is a commutative ring, $(f+g)(k) = f(k)+g(k)$, and $(\iota(c)h)(k) = c\,h(k)$ ([[lem-laurent-series-ring]]).
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/thm-laurent-ordered-field.md-216-
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/thm-laurent-ordered-field.md-217-[L3] For nonzero $f, g \in K$: $fg \ne 0_K$ with $\operatorname{lc}(fg) = \operatorname{lc}(f)\operatorname{lc}(g)$; $-f \ne 0_K$ with $v(-f) = v(f)$ and $\operatorname{lc}(-f) = -\operatorname{lc}(f)$; if $v(f) < v(g)$ then $f+g \ne 0_K$ with $v(f+g) = v(f)$ and $\operatorname{lc}(f+g) = \operatorname{lc}(f)$; and if $v(f) = v(g)$ with $\operatorname{lc}(f) + \operatorname{lc}(g) \ne 0$ then $f+g \ne 0_K$ with $\operatorname{lc}(f+g) = \operatorname{lc}(f) + \operatorname{lc}(g)$ ([[lem-laurent-valuation]]).
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/thm-laurent-ordered-field.md-218-
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/thm-laurent-ordered-field.md-219-[L4] $K$ is a field ([[thm-laurent-series-field]], [[def-field]]).
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/thm-laurent-ordered-field.md-220-
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/thm-laurent-ordered-field.md:221:[L5] An ordered field is a field with a subset $P$ satisfying (O1) trichotomy, for each $x$ exactly one of $x \in P$, $x = 0$, $-x \in P$, and (O2) closure of $P$ under addition and multiplication; the order is then $a < b :\iff b - a \in P$ ([[def-ordered-field]]). For $n \ge 1$, $n \cdot 1_F$ is the $n$-fold sum of $1_F$, and $0 \cdot 1_F = 0$ ([[def-archimedean-field]]).
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/thm-laurent-ordered-field.md-222-
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/thm-laurent-ordered-field.md-223-[L6] $\mathbb{R}$ is an ordered field: exactly one of $x > 0$, $x = 0$, $x < 0$ holds for each real $x$, and sums and products of positive reals are positive ([[thm-reals-ordered-field]], [[def-ordered-field]]).
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/thm-laurent-ordered-field.md-224-
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/thm-laurent-ordered-field.md-225-[L7] $|x| = x$ when $x \ge 0$ and $|x| = -x$ when $x < 0$, in any ordered field and in $\mathbb{R}$ ([[def-abs-value]]).
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/thm-laurent-ordered-field.md-226-
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/thm-laurent-ordered-field.md-227-[L8] Induction: a property holding at $0$ and inherited from $n$ to $n+1$ holds at every natural number ([[thm-induction-principle]], [[def-natural-numbers]]).
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/thm-laurent-ordered-field.md-228-
research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/thm-laurent-ordered-field.md-229-[L9] The order on $\mathbb{Z}$ is total, so for $p, q \in \mathbb{Z}$ exactly one of $p < q$, $p = q$, $q < p$ holds ([[thm-int-ordered-ring]]).
