research/audit/wave6-certifier-tasks/thm-laurent-ordered-field.md-249-4.1 Let $f \ne 0_K$. If $f \in P$ then $f > 0_K$ by [step 3.1], so $|f| = f$ by [L7], and $\operatorname{lc}(|f|) = \operatorname{lc}(f) = \lvert \operatorname{lc}(f)\rvert$ since $\operatorname{lc}(f) > 0$. Otherwise $-f \in P$ by [step 1.1], so $f < 0_K$ and $|f| = -f$, whence $|f| \ne 0_K$, $v(|f|) = v(f)$ and $\operatorname{lc}(|f|) = -\operatorname{lc}(f) = \lvert\operatorname{lc}(f)\rvert$, again positive. In both cases $v(|f|) = v(f)$ and $\operatorname{lc}(|f|) = \lvert\operatorname{lc}(f)\rvert > 0$. [step 1.1, step 3.1, L3, L7]
