research/audit/wave6-real-analysis-laurent.proof-contracts.json:1870:          "quote": "Every sequence $(f^{(n)})_{n \\in \\mathbb{N}}$ in $K = \\mathbb{R}((t^{-1}))$ that\nis Cauchy in $K$ ([[def-sequences-in-an-ordered-field]]) converges in $K$. That\nis, the ordered field $K$ of [[thm-laurent-ordered-field]] is **sequentially\nCauchy complete**.",
