research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-cex-zero-times-infinity-indeterminate.prompt.md:366:**Given:** The canonical naturals $\iota(n) = n \cdot 1_{\mathbb{R}}$; the sequence $x_k := 1/\iota(k+1)$; for a real $c > 0$ the sequence $y^{(c)}_k := c\,\iota(k+1)$; and the sequence $z_k := \iota(k+1)\,\iota(k+1)$.
