research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-270-1. $P$ is a positive cone on $K$, so $(K, P)$ is an ordered field
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-271-   ([[def-ordered-field]]), and $f < g$ holds exactly when $g - f \ne 0_K$ and
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-272-   $\operatorname{lc}(g - f) > 0$.
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-273-2. For $f \ne 0_K$ the absolute value ([[def-abs-value]]) satisfies
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-274-   $|f| \ne 0_K$, $v(|f|) = v(f)$ and
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-275-   $\operatorname{lc}(|f|) = \lvert \operatorname{lc}(f) \rvert > 0$.
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-276-3. The map $\iota : \mathbb{R} \to K$ sending $c$ to the series with value $c$
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-277-   at index $0$ is an injective ring homomorphism with $\iota(c) \in P$ exactly
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log:278:   when $c > 0$; and the canonical naturals of $K$ are
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-279-   $n \cdot 1_K = \iota(n \cdot 1_{\mathbb{R}})$ for every $n \in \mathbb{N}$.
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-280-
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-281-## Facts & Assumptions
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-282-
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-283-**Given:** $K$ with its valuation $v$, leading coefficient $\operatorname{lc}$, constants $\iota(c)$ and the set $P$ above.
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-284-
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-285-[L1] For nonzero $h \in K$, $h(k) = 0$ for $k < v(h)$ and $h(v(h)) = \operatorname{lc}(h) \ne 0$; $\iota(c)$ is $c$ at index $0$ and $0$ elsewhere; $1_K = \iota(1)$ ([[def-formal-laurent-series]]).
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-286-
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-287-[L2] $K$ is a commutative ring, $(f+g)(k) = f(k)+g(k)$, and $(\iota(c)h)(k) = c\,h(k)$ ([[lem-laurent-series-ring]]).
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-288-
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-289-[L3] For nonzero $f, g \in K$: $fg \ne 0_K$ with $\operatorname{lc}(fg) = \operatorname{lc}(f)\operatorname{lc}(g)$; $-f \ne 0_K$ with $v(-f) = v(f)$ and $\operatorname{lc}(-f) = -\operatorname{lc}(f)$; if $v(f) < v(g)$ then $f+g \ne 0_K$ with $v(f+g) = v(f)$ and $\operatorname{lc}(f+g) = \operatorname{lc}(f)$; and if $v(f) = v(g)$ with $\operatorname{lc}(f) + \operatorname{lc}(g) \ne 0$ then $f+g \ne 0_K$ with $\operatorname{lc}(f+g) = \operatorname{lc}(f) + \operatorname{lc}(g)$ ([[lem-laurent-valuation]]).
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-290-
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-291-[L4] $K$ is a field ([[thm-laurent-series-field]], [[def-field]]).
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-292-
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log:293:[L5] An ordered field is a field with a subset $P$ satisfying (O1) trichotomy, for each $x$ exactly one of $x \in P$, $x = 0$, $-x \in P$, and (O2) closure of $P$ under addition and multiplication; the order is then $a < b :\iff b - a \in P$ ([[def-ordered-field]]). For $n \ge 1$, $n \cdot 1_F$ is the $n$-fold sum of $1_F$, and $0 \cdot 1_F = 0$ ([[def-archimedean-field]]).
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-294-
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-295-[L6] $\mathbb{R}$ is an ordered field: exactly one of $x > 0$, $x = 0$, $x < 0$ holds for each real $x$, and sums and products of positive reals are positive ([[thm-reals-ordered-field]], [[def-ordered-field]]).
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-296-
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-297-[L7] $|x| = x$ when $x \ge 0$ and $|x| = -x$ when $x < 0$, in any ordered field and in $\mathbb{R}$ ([[def-abs-value]]).
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-298-
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-299-[L8] Induction: a property holding at $0$ and inherited from $n$ to $n+1$ holds at every natural number ([[thm-induction-principle]], [[def-natural-numbers]]).
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-300-
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-301-[L9] The order on $\mathbb{Z}$ is total, so for $p, q \in \mathbb{Z}$ exactly one of $p < q$, $p = q$, $q < p$ holds ([[thm-int-ordered-ring]]).
--
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-321-4.1 Let $f \ne 0_K$. If $f \in P$ then $f > 0_K$ by [step 3.1], so $|f| = f$ by [L7], and $\operatorname{lc}(|f|) = \operatorname{lc}(f) = \lvert \operatorname{lc}(f)\rvert$ since $\operatorname{lc}(f) > 0$. Otherwise $-f \in P$ by [step 1.1], so $f < 0_K$ and $|f| = -f$, whence $|f| \ne 0_K$, $v(|f|) = v(f)$ and $\operatorname{lc}(|f|) = -\operatorname{lc}(f) = \lvert\operatorname{lc}(f)\rvert$, again positive. In both cases $v(|f|) = v(f)$ and $\operatorname{lc}(|f|) = \lvert\operatorname{lc}(f)\rvert > 0$. [step 1.1, step 3.1, L3, L7]
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-322-
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-323-5.1 Clause 1 is [step 3.1], clause 2 is [step 4.1], and clause 3 is [step 2.2] with [step 2.3]. [step 3.1, step 2.2, step 4.1, step 2.3] ∎
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-324-
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-325-## Remarks
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-326-
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-327-- **The order compares lowest terms, and only those.** By clause 1, deciding $f < g$ means finding the least index at which $f$ and $g$ differ and comparing the two coefficients there. Every later coefficient is irrelevant, which is why $\iota(c) > t^{-1}$ for every positive real $c$, however small, and why the order is not the coefficientwise one.
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log-328-
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/certifier-thm-laurent-ordered-field.log:329:- **$\mathbb{R}$ sits inside $K$ as an ordered subfield, and that is all clause 3 says.** It does not say that $\mathbb{R}$ is cofinal in $K$, and indeed it is not: the computation used for the canonical naturals in [[lem-laurent-non-archimedean]] applies verbatim to every constant, since $v(t) = -1 < 0 = v(\iota(c))$ for every $c \ne 0$, so $\iota(c) < t$ for every real $c$. The identification $n \cdot 1_K = \iota(n \cdot 1_{\mathbb{R}})$ is recorded because the Archimedean property is a statement about the canonical naturals ([[def-archimedean-field]]), and it is the bridge between those and the constant series.
