research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/fs-limsup-additive.md-2310-1.1 Since $\Lambda + M$ is defined, exactly one of the following three situations holds: at least one of $\Lambda$, $M$ equals $+\infty$, and then the other is $\ne -\infty$; both are real; or neither equals $+\infty$ and at least one equals $-\infty$. Both the hypothesis and the conclusion of claim 1 are unchanged by exchanging the two sequences, so in the third situation it may be assumed that $\Lambda = -\infty$. [given, L2, L3]
