research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-limits-apply.log-5261-The witness below has a nonempty $\operatorname{SL}(x)$ with a greatest element,
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-limits-apply.log-5262-so the failure is not that the real set is empty: it is that the greatest element
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-limits-apply.log-5263-of $\operatorname{SL}(x)$ is $0$ while $\limsup_k x_k = +\infty$. The dominant
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-limits-apply.log-5264-behaviour of the sequence is invisible to $\operatorname{SL}(x)$ and is recorded
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-limits-apply.log-5265-only by $\overline{\operatorname{SL}}(x)$ ([[def-extended-limits]]).
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-limits-apply.log-5266-
