research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-limsup-submultiplicative.md:2619:**Given:** A complete ordered field $F$; write $A = \{\, n \cdot 1_F : n \ge 1 \,\}$ for the set of its canonical naturals.
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-limsup-submultiplicative.md-2620-
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-limsup-submultiplicative.md-2621-[L1] Least-upper-bound property: every nonempty $S \subseteq F$ that is bounded above has a least upper bound $\sup S \in F$ ([[def-complete-ordered-field]]).
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-limsup-submultiplicative.md-2622-
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-limsup-submultiplicative.md-2623-[L2] Each canonical natural satisfies $n \cdot 1_F > 0$, one has $(n+1) \cdot 1_F = n \cdot 1_F + 1_F$, and $(n+1) \cdot 1_F > n \cdot 1_F$ ([[lem-of-naturals-positive]]).
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-limsup-submultiplicative.md-2624-
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-limsup-submultiplicative.md-2625-[L3] $0 < 1_F$ ([[cor-of-one-positive]]).
