research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-alpha-a3-concurrence.log-3387-## Mathematical audit record
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-alpha-a3-concurrence.log-3388-
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-alpha-a3-concurrence.log-3389-- `lem-laurent-series-ring`: the support translation to `N`, finite convolution bounds, triple-convolution associativity, closure, monomial shifts, constants, identity, and ring assembly are correct. The finite-sum reassociation claim follows directly from the cited field laws within the standing 30-second allowance.
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-alpha-a3-concurrence.log-3390-- `lem-laurent-valuation`: the unique contribution at the product's least index and every sum/cancellation case are exhaustive and correct.
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-alpha-a3-concurrence.log-3391-- `thm-laurent-series-field`: the factorization `f=iota(c)t^{-p}(1-u)`, support of every `u^n`, coefficientwise finite definition of `g`, convolution reindexing, and the identity `(1-u)g=1` were checked at every index, including `k<0`, `k=0`, and `k>=1`.
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-alpha-a3-concurrence.log:3392:- `thm-laurent-ordered-field`: positive-cone trichotomy and closure, the constant embedding, canonical naturals, and absolute-value clauses are correct. W6-RALA-001 concerns only the source of the canonical-natural notation.
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-alpha-a3-concurrence.log-3393-- `lem-laurent-non-archimedean`: `t` dominates every canonical natural, the monomial chain is strictly decreasing and coinitial among positives, and both directions of the coefficient/valuation threshold estimate are correct, including `h=0` and the strict endpoint distinction.
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-alpha-a3-concurrence.log-3394-- `cor-laurent-not-lub-complete`: both the abstract contrapositive and the concrete canonical-naturals witness are valid. Every upper bound has negative valuation, and halving its leading coefficient yields a strictly smaller upper bound.
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-alpha-a3-concurrence.log-3395-- `thm-laurent-cauchy-complete`: Cauchyness at `t^{-(k+1)}` freezes every coefficient through index `k`; the least stages `N_k` are monotone; the coefficientwise limit has a uniform lower support bound from `k=0`; and the monomial coinitiality clause converts coefficient stabilization back to convergence for every positive epsilon. No choice principle is used.
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-alpha-a3-concurrence.log-3396-- `cor-laurent-nested-intervals`: nestedness makes the left endpoints Cauchy, Cauchy completeness supplies the limit, closed endpoint inequalities retain it in every interval, and shrinking length gives uniqueness. W6-RALA-003 concerns only total-order citation precision.
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-alpha-a3-concurrence.log-3397-- `cex-laurent-nested-intervals-empty`: the intervals are nonempty and nested. A common positive point would have valuation at least 1 from all real-constant upper endpoints and valuation below 1 from all multiples of `t^{-1}`; this is impossible. Each length has a nonzero coefficient at index 0, so it never becomes smaller than `t^{-1}`.
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-alpha-a3-concurrence.log-3398-
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-alpha-a3-concurrence.log-3399-No mathematical falsehood was found in either definition, any Statement, proof, counterexample, or Remark.
