research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-laurent-apply.log-19246--[L5] An ordered field is a field with a subset $P$ satisfying (O1) trichotomy, for each $x$ exactly one of $x \in P$, $x = 0$, $-x \in P$, and (O2) closure of $P$ under addition and multiplication; the order is then $a < b :\iff b - a \in P$, and $n \cdot 1_F$ denotes the $n$-fold sum of $1_F$, with $0 \cdot 1_F = 0$ ([[def-ordered-field]]).
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-laurent-apply.log:19247:+[L5] An ordered field is a field with a subset $P$ satisfying (O1) trichotomy, for each $x$ exactly one of $x \in P$, $x = 0$, $-x \in P$, and (O2) closure of $P$ under addition and multiplication; the order is then $a < b :\iff b - a \in P$ ([[def-ordered-field]]). For $n \ge 1$, $n \cdot 1_F$ is the $n$-fold sum of $1_F$, and $0 \cdot 1_F = 0$ ([[def-archimedean-field]]).
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-laurent-apply.log-19248- 
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-laurent-apply.log-19249- [L6] $\mathbb{R}$ is an ordered field: exactly one of $x > 0$, $x = 0$, $x < 0$ holds for each real $x$, and sums and products of positive reals are positive ([[thm-reals-ordered-field]], [[def-ordered-field]]).
