research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-laurent-apply.log-21564- 
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-laurent-apply.log-21565--- **The order compares lowest terms, and only those.** By clause 1, deciding
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-laurent-apply.log-21566--  $f < g$ means finding the least index at which $f$ and $g$ differ and
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-laurent-apply.log-21567--  comparing the two coefficients there. Every later coefficient is irrelevant,
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-laurent-apply.log-21568--  which is why $\iota(c) > t^{-1}$ for every positive real $c$, however small,
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-laurent-apply.log-21569--  and why the order is not the coefficientwise one.
