research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-laurent-apply.log:22829:+- `W6-RALA-001`, `thm-laurent-ordered-field`: the old `[L5]` attributed both the positive-cone definition and canonical-natural notation to `def-ordered-field`. The new `[L5]` keeps the positive-cone and order clause under `[[def-ordered-field]]` and states separately: “For $n \ge 1$, $n \cdot 1_F$ is the $n$-fold sum of $1_F$, and $0 \cdot 1_F = 0$,” citing `[[def-archimedean-field]]`. That target's Definition gives exactly the $n$-fold-sum and zero clauses. `def-archimedean-field` was added to `deps`.
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-laurent-apply.log-22830-+- `W6-RALA-002`, `thm-laurent-cauchy-complete`: the old `[L6]` asserted totality of the natural order while citing only its definitions, induction, and the natural-to-integer embedding. The new `[L6]` attributes totality to `[[thm-nat-linear-order]]`, whose Statement says that the defined relation is a linear (total) order, while retaining the original exact sources for induction and the embedding. `thm-nat-linear-order` was added to `deps`.
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-laurent-apply.log-22831-+- `W6-RALA-003`, `cor-laurent-nested-intervals`: the same unsupported totality clause in `[L5]` now cites `[[thm-nat-linear-order]]`, with the induction clause left under `[[thm-induction-principle]]` and `[[def-natural-numbers]]`. `thm-nat-linear-order` was added to `deps`.
